 **Version:** 3.0  
 **Status:** Complete  
-**Last Updated:** October 5, 2026
+**Last Updated:** October 22, 2026
 
 > **Content-free hash-only core (Slice 1, Plan B).** `POST /events` is the sole ingestion door and accepts a content-free `canonical.HashOnlyEnvelope` — locators, HMAC pseudonyms, and precomputed leaf hashes only. Raw content never reaches the core; producers (a future content sidecar, or a BYO client) compute the hashes before submitting. See [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) and [SEPARATION_OF_CONCERNS_CANONICAL_HASHING_SPEC.md](../plans/SEPARATION_OF_CONCERNS_CANONICAL_HASHING_SPEC.md) for the full contract.
 
@@ -412,7 +412,9 @@ Batch details and the ordered event list. **This is not a tamper check.**
 
 The only endpoint that consults the chain is [`GET /events/{id}/verify`](#get-eventsidverify) (`chain_anchor`). To be sure the answer is a live read, pass `?fresh=true` and assert `chain_anchor.source == "chain"`.
 
-**Errors:** 400, 401, 403, 404, 500, 503
+*(changed 2026-10-22)* A failed read of the batch, or of its event list, is HTTP 500 `{"error":"retrieval_error","message":"Failed to retrieve batch"}`. The handler does not return 200 without `event_ids`.
+
+**Errors:** 400, 401, 403, 404, 500 (`retrieval_error`), 503
 
